WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:05.167
-Our next guest has his comedy
special, "Perfectly Stupid,"

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:08.901
available now at
perfectlystupid.com.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:13.000
Please welcome the very funny
Kurt Braunohler, everybody.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:23.367
-Hello. Thank you.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:27.100
So, I have two kids,

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:32.234
which is so much more than one.

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:34.434
I don't know if I like
who I am with two kids.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.701
I love the kids.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:39.300
But, recently,
I screamed at my entire family

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.968
at the dinner table, "I don't
care if everyone's crying.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:46.534
I'm eating."

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:51.067
I don't want to be that man.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.968
And when I had one kid,
if someone asked me,

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.067
"Hey, should I have kids?",
I was like, "Yeah."

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.767
But now, when I have two kids,
if someone's like,

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.834
"Should I have kids?",
I'm like, "Don't talk to me.

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:01.200
I have 15 minutes to
drink this vodka soda

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.934
before going to bed,
because every minute

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.434
that he sleeps
that I don't sleep,

00:01:04.434 --> 00:01:06.734
he gets stronger than me!"

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.534
But I want to be a good dad.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.801
I'm trying.
I'll tell you a story.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.534
There's a gas station
near my house.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:23.601
It has a small, handwritten sign
on one of the pumps that says,

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:26.033
"Please replace nozzle to pump

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.434
before driving away with it."

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.968
And I thought that was funny.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.534
You know, I laughed at
all these idiots

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:35.868
who were driving away with
the pump still in their car.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:40.901
And so, when I drove away with
the pump in my car...

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.434
I was bashful,

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.400
a little embarrassed,
you might say.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.300
I didn't even know
I did it, okay?

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:52.734
Hopped in my car, blasting
my meditation app, and just

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:55.701
took off, yanked it
right out of the thing,

00:01:55.701 --> 00:02:00.400
and immediately pulled an
illegal four-lane U-turn.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.801
All the oncoming traffic
was like...

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:02.901
[ Imitates horns honking ]

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:06.567
And I was like,
"Oh, screw you, nerds!

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.801
It's a U-turn!"

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.434
I gave them all
the middle finger,

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:16.267
meanwhile spewing gasoline
across the street.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.934
And then I made a right and
I got on an even bigger highway,

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.267
started going very fast.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.067
And, mind you, I have a tail.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.567
Just...

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:26.567
And a big white pickup truck
pulls up next to me

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:31.968
and starts honking at me,
and I was like, "It's a U-turn!"

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:33.467
And he's like,
"Roll your window down."

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:34.834
I was like, "What?"

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:39.701
He was like, "You drove
away with the pump in your car."

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:44.767
And I was like, "Oh, you drove
away with the -- Aah!

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.801
So I did."

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.033
And then I was very embarrassed.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.467
I didn't know what to do.

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.334
I'm on a highway,

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.667
so I just pulled over
to the side of the road.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:57.033
And he pulled over, too.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:03:00.100
And then I got out of my car,
and he got out of his car.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.234
And, mind you,
I'm deeply embarrassed.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.567
It's essentially like
I just crapped my pants,

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.701
and he, like, followed me
into the bathroom like,

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.567
"Hey, did you
crap your pants, man?

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.667
Hey, how much
crap is in your pants?

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:16.467
Hey, why you think
you crapped your pants earlier?"

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.734
And I was like,
"What do you want?"

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:21.901
And he said, "Do you need help?"

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.701
And I realized,
I had a choice as dad.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:27.434
You know, I could act like men
have acted for millennia.

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.901
I could lash out like
a wounded animal.

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:31.801
Or I could be vulnerable

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:35.033
and admit, "Yes, I screwed up
and I do need help."

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:36.868
And so I looked
at this man offering

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:40.968
this olive branch of help
and I said, "No!"

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:53.367
And then I got in
my car and drove away.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:56.100
And I -- You know,
at first, I looked at the car

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.400
and I realized,
"Oh, I have gas --

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.601
I pulled it out of my car

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.767
and I was like,
"This is filled with gas still."

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:04.400
What would be very
useful would be a pickup truck,

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.801
but that guy just -- I just told
him to go screw himself.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:12.133
So then I had to walk with it
in my arms along the highway

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:15.033
like a big dead snake
back to where

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:20.167
both gas-station managers are
standing outside waiting for me.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:23.334
And then I just laid it
at their feet.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:24.734
And I was like,
"What do we do now?"

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.133
And they're like,
"We don't know.

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:29.234
There's no form for this, pal."

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:32.601
Turns out, it costs $350,

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:35.601
which is honestly a lot less
than I expected.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:36.834
And you know what?

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.100
They're designed to
just pop right off,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.267
so you can just do it.

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.734
It doesn't matter.
You can just do it.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.467
Honestly, if you turned it
into a comedy bit,

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.234
maybe you'll get on
"The Tonight Show."

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:52.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.634
♪♪

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.033
-Wow! Uh-huh.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.467
Come on. That's unbelievable.

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.567
Kurt Braunohler!

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.367
Kurt Braunohler --
"Perfectly Stupid"

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:07.234
is available at
perfectlystupid.com.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:08.300
We'll be right back, everybody.

